# mgstrong.msg - the wage strongbox in Moriarty's office (mgstrong.ssl). One entry per line; no braces in comments.

# 100 to 103: look (locked, unlocked) and examine (wages inside, wages gone).
{100}{}{You see an iron strongbox. It is locked.}
{101}{}{You see an iron strongbox.}
{102}{}{It is bolted to the floor beside the bed, where its owner can hear it breathe.}
{103}{}{It is bolted to the floor beside the bed. It sounds emptier than it used to.}

# 120 to 123: the lock picked, or not.
{120}{}{Something inside the lock gives up. The strongbox is unlocked.}
{121}{}{The lock does not move. Moriarty bought this one to last.}
{122}{}{Your pick jumps out of the keyhole and nearly out of your hand. The lock has not noticed you.}
{123}{}{It is not locked.}

# 140 to 143: the key, traps.
{140}{}{Moriarty's key fits. The strongbox is unlocked.}
{141}{}{You turn the key. The strongbox is locked again.}
{142}{}{Close the lid before you lock it.}
{143}{}{You find no traps. The owner sleeps an arm's length away and trusts that.}

# 200 to 212: the choice, hosted by the box.
{200}{}{Inside: a ledger, and two paper packets tied with string. One is marked GOB. One is marked NOVA. A hundred and eighty dollars between them, and by the ledger, fifteen years of somebody waiting for it.}
{201}{}{[Take the money.]}
{202}{}{[Read the ledger.]}
{203}{}{[Close the lid.]}
{210}{}{You pocket both packets. It is the lightest hundred and eighty dollars you have ever taken from two people at once. The names on the paper do not come off.}
{211}{}{Moriarty's hand, neat as a tombstone. Every week: wages owed. Every week: room, board, breakage, sundries. The sums come out in his favor every single time. Gob's column starts fifteen years back.}
{212}{}{[Done.]}
